  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Wisconsin has recorded $202M in federal contract obligations for FY2027 to date. The state has 1,368 awards and an average award size of $148K. Obligations fell 95.9% year over year. Historical totals show large swings: FY22 totaled $5.6B, FY23 totaled $5.7B, FY24 totaled $9.9B, FY25 totaled $7.4B, and FY26 totaled $4.9B. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer in FY2027 to date with $121M in obligations, followed by the Department of Health and Human Services with $45.1M and the Department of Agriculture with $12.8M. OPTUMSERVE HEALTH SERVICES, INC. is the largest vendor in FY2027 to date with $85.6M, followed by WISCONSIN PHYSICIANS SERVICE INSURANCE CORP. with $41.8M. Offices of Physicians (except Mental Health Specialists) is the largest industry by obligation with $83.4M, and Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers follow with $41.8M. All figures are contract obligations; current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated is federal procurement in Wisconsin this year?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs accounted for a large share with $121M in obligations. OPTUMSERVE HEALTH SERVICES, INC. accounted for $85.6M of obligations and WISCONSIN PHYSICIANS SERVICE INSURANCE CORP. accounted for $41.8M. Offices of Physicians (except Mental Health Specialists) accounted for $83.4M of industry obligations."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How have Wisconsin obligations trended over recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "FY24 was the peak in this series with $9.9B in obligations. FY26 obligations fell to $4.9B and FY27 to date stands at $202M. Obligations fell 95.9% year over year for the current fiscal-year-to-date comparison."
      }
    ]
